# Credentials — NEVER commit these.
# A service account key in a public repo is full admin access to the whole
# Firebase project: every charity's details, the CRM, the lot.
#
# The repository is public, so this file is the thing standing between that key
# and the open internet. Two patterns, not one, because serviceAccount.json.json
# exists in this folder and a single leading-anchored pattern would miss a copy
# saved under another name.
serviceAccount*.json
*serviceAccount*.json
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Local noise
node_modules/
.firebase/
*-debug.log
firebase-debug.*.log
test-results/
.vercel/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Built by the publish workflow, never committed.
site/
